19. What is Amazon DocumentDB and when would you recommend it?
Answer:
Amazon DocumentDB is a managed document database service designed to be compatible with MongoDB workloads.
It stores data in a document-oriented model, typically using JSON-like documents.
I would consider DocumentDB when:
The application uses a document data model.
MongoDB compatibility is required.
The organization wants a managed AWS database.
High availability and scalability are required.
The application doesn't require features that are unsupported by DocumentDB.
I would not automatically choose DocumentDB just because the application uses MongoDB. I would first verify MongoDB compatibility, supported features, performance requirements and application dependencies.
